# Source: https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
#   https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/919
# Symptom: BED12 blockStarts list is not in strictly ascending order; col 12
#   values should increase monotonically (each exon starts after the previous).
#   A common source is a naive sort applied only to chromStart that scrambles
#   blockStarts and blockSizes together, or a GFF-to-BED converter that emits
#   CDS blocks in annotation order rather than genomic order.  Tools that build
#   an exon model from blockStarts in order will produce overlapping or inverted
#   exons.
# Format: chrom start end name score strand thickStart thickEnd itemRgb blockCount blockSizes blockStarts
chr1	1000	5000	gene1	0	+	1000	5000	0	3	200,300,400	2000,500,100
chr2	10000	20000	gene2	0	-	10000	20000	0	3	100,200,300	5000,2000,0
